  "description": "The Dallas Rangemaster: one germanium PNP (an OC44) on a negative supply (positive ground, V- at -9 V). C1 (5 nF) into its low input impedance makes it a treble booster; the volume pot VR1 is the collector load. Values and refs from ElectroSmash's \"Dallas Rangemaster Treble Booster Analysis\" (electrosmash.com/dallas-rangemaster), as the Rangemaster starter, with our own OC44 fit (hFE about 92). Put it first: it needs the guitar's pickup driving it.",
